 ; Shortens the recording lock that delays NR start. Default false; applies to the next frame; logged as inline_reuse.
 NrInlineReuse=false
 ; GPU-armed inline handoff (Mochizuki). The side queue waits for this frame's game list to start, watches the
-; capture flag on the GPU with a bounded budget, then starts Vulkan without a CPU verification round trip.
-; Missed capture selects the original frame and requests history reset at reclamation; NR still launches.
-; Known deferred risk: a claimed but unfinished input copy may race NR on cap/abort (see docs/architecture/nr-capture-proof-deferral.md).
-; Default true; applies to the next frame; logged as handoff.
+; capture flag on the GPU with a bounded budget. The worker verifies its completed readback before starting Vulkan.
+; Missed capture skips NR, selects the original frame and resets history before the next enqueue.
+; Default true; applies to the next frame; logged as handoff. The worker fence wait is outside the recording lock.
 ; When true, NrCaptureBackoff is bypassed; NrInlineReuse still applies. When false, the spin options below are inactive.
 NrGpuHandoff=true
 ; Inline spin options (Mochizuki, GPU-armed handoff only; NrSpinPollDelay defaults to 16, others off; apply to the next frame; logged in NrFrameDiag as spin_*/watch_*).
